      "source": [
        "\n",
        "# Gemma-3 VisBias — Base vs V2 LoRA\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook evaluates the same two models on a race-focused VisBias adaptation:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Base:** `google/gemma-3-12b-it`\n",
        "- **Tuned:** Base + saved V2 valence-controlled LoRA\n",
        "\n",
        "The implementation follows the design in Elias's `visbias.py`:\n",
        "\n",
        "- occupations: CEO, basketball player, cook, doctor, firefighter, lawyer, nurse\n",
        "- gender: female / male\n",
        "- race: black / white\n",
        "- matched Black–White image pairs\n",
        "- two comparison attributes:\n",
        "  - income\n",
        "  - education\n",
        "- **A/B image order is reversed for every comparison unit**\n",
        "- valid answers: `A`, `B`, or `Cannot determine`\n",
        "- all raw responses saved incrementally to Drive and safely resumable\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook also supports the long-description task and the VisBias race stereotype lexicon,\n",
        "but the default run focuses on the **1,000 matched Black–White image pairs** requested by the team.\n",
        "\n",
        "> Important: 1,000 matched pairs × 2 attributes × 2 image orders = **4,000 comparison calls/model**.\n",
        "> Base + V2 therefore means **8,000 multimodal generations**. The notebook is resumable after every task.\n"
      ]
    },
